<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Capture of Hormuz (1622)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1622</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hormuz">Hormuz</a> in 1622 was the expulsion of the Portuguese from the island fortress at the entrance of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Persian Gulf</a> by forces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a> with English naval assistance. It ended more than a century of Portuguese control over Gulf trade. The victory brought the empire under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbas-i-of-persia">Shah Abbas I</a> close to its maximum extent.</p></div>
